settings.definition_quote:
We say the loss is \emph{graph-structured} with respect to $\cG$ if the
  expected loss for criterion $i$ depends only on the state of its local
  neighborhood $\cN(i)$. Formally, there exist local feature maps
  $\phi_i\colon [0, 1]^{|\cN(i)|} \to \Rset^{d_i}$ and parameters
  $\btheta^*_i \in \Rset^{d_i}$ such that:
  \begin{equation}
    \label{eq:1}
    \mu_i(\bs) = \tri*{ \phi_i(\bs|_{\cN(i)}), \btheta^*_i }.
  \end{equation}
